# ZONEMD (Zone Metadata) Record
# ==============================
# ZONEMD provides metadata about the DNS zone itself, including information
# about entities authorized to make changes to the zone.
#
# Format: The file is JSON with:
#   - version: ZONEMD version (currently 1)
#   - policy: Authorization policy
#     - allowed: List of domains/hosts allowed to make changes
#     - disallowed: List of domains/hosts NOT allowed to make changes
#   - members: Contact information for allowed entities
#
# The ZONEMD record in DNS is created by hashing this JSON using SHA-384.
#
# NOTE: Authoritative ZONEMD record is defined in security/bind9/trigger.zone
# This file is provided for web servers that serve .well-known/ for compatibility.
#
# For more information: RFC 8901 (ZONEMD)
# https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8901
#
# To generate the DNS record:
#   sha384sum <(echo -n '{"version":1,"policy":{"allowed":["github.com"],"disallowed":[]},"members":{"github.com":{"contact":"https://github.com/hyperpolymath/trigger/issues"}}}')
#   _zonemd IN ZONEMD 1 <SHA-384 hash in base64>
